Z||000000||fiero56||06-09-2000||08:43 AM||||car: Formula, ('88 v-6 5-speed)<P>I replaced both tranny mounts(stock rubber type from FS), and also added an ultimate dogbone from the FS. This greatly reduced the engine movement I had, but there is still more than I would like. I am not looking to race this car or anything, but when I'm driving and mash the gas, I want the car to leap ahead, instead of all this "bouncing" the engine does. Is there a stiffer rubber mount I could use? Something that only "gives" under heavier pressures. Polly? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||06-09-2000||09:49 AM||||i have seen the poly mounts at west coast fiero's site... but i would be willing to bet that you could also get them from Prothane!||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||06-09-2000||02:01 PM||||you can get the bushings from Prothane and Energy suspension or Paeco (Delrin) but you have to either make or buy the "mounts" for the bushings.. they take a square stock fit bushings re engineer it to fit a round poly bushing...<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||06-09-2000||04:45 PM||||Am I going to notice a large amount of engine vibration with the polly? I don't like engine movement, but this car is also my daily driver.||||reg||1
Z||000004||chris west||06-10-2000||10:40 AM||||Well maybe we can start another ink war! The polyurethane will add some shake to the car at idle but it will go away when the idle is brought up to 1200 or so.This mount also helps the axel rapup on the drivers side that you get eith stock mounts.<BR>Chris<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||06-10-2000||10:21 PM||||WOW! you got an answer from the Man himself...   yep what Chris said!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">your rear view mirror will shake at the light but not enought to be neuseating (sp) ||||reg||1
Z||000006||HYPTNOTiSE||06-11-2000||05:03 PM||||If you're looking for a new motor mount, try MORSE86@AOL.COM. Darrell made me a motor mount with a poly bushing. It's the same exact poly bushing used in the dog bone, so you dont have to worry about searching all over for an odd size bushing, if you ever need to replace it. He doesn't make tranny mounts at this time, and i'm going to order them from chris west.  but they're 55 bucks a peice.  Darrel made me a motor mount, and a custom solid mount with heim joints, to take the place of the stupid shock absorber thingy for 60 bucks shipping included.  Darrell's prices are as always very good. He's comming out with tranny mounts soon, but he's backed up with projects, and if he has anymore, his wife will probably divorce him  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks<BR>Mike LeCompte||||reg||3
